WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.500
Fasting is put to the test
for a number of diseases.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.340
Does it help?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.540
Watch the video to find out,
and check out the Doctor’s Note below

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.634
for other videos on the topic.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:21.596
"Fasting for Rheumatoid Arthritis
and Autoimmune Disease"

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.320
Alan Goldhamer is the founder
of the TrueNorth Health Center

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.000
in Santa Rosa, California, which has
fasted 10,000 people for conditions

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.960
ranging from diabetes and cardiovascular
disease to autoimmune diseases.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.440
He noted that conditions that
seem to be tied to dietary excess

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.140
tend to respond predictably
to the use of fasting

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.160
followed by a health-promoting diet,
which he describes as a low salt,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.420
all plant, high fiber, low fat,
low protein, and low sugar diet.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.100
This approach offers people
an option to eliminate the cause

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.580
of lifestyle diseases often to
the point where the medication

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.420
is no longer needed, in contrast
to conventional medicine,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.600
which is more about the
suppression of the symptoms

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.640
associated with the disease, rather
than removing the underlying root cause.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.480
Goldhamer put it this way:
If you treat high blood pressure

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.780
or type 2 diabetes or autoimmune
disease medically, they'll tell you,

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.960
"You'll be on these medications
the rest of your life."

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.220
That’s them in effect promising
you, if you follow their advice

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.420
to the letter, “you will be
sick the rest of your life.”

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.500
Preliminary data suggests fasting
may benefit metabolic diseases,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.040
pain syndromes, high blood pressure,
chronic inflammatory diseases,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.860
allergic diseases, and
psychosomatic disorders,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.860
but the highest level of evidence
we have for the benefits of fasting

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.960
are in regards to rheumatic diseases:

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.160
autoimmune inflammatory joint
diseases, like rheumatoid arthritis.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.740
Nearly a century ago it was
written that “diet treatment

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.840
is not generally recognized
by the medical profession…

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.680
as one of the weapons with
which to attack [such diseases].”

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.740
This attitude persisted
until relatively recently,

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.800
but a systematic review of
controlled trials has since

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.720
“shown a statistically and clinically
significant beneficial long-term effect.”

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.920
Rheumatoid arthritis has a
well-known genetic component,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.340
but the concordance rate, the chance
that a pair of identical twins

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.540
both get it when one has
it is probably under 30%,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.200
despite having the
same genes, leaving 70%

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.020
to be explained by non-genetic factors.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.440
Even if we don't know exactly
what those factors are,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.940
“fasting [has been compared] to
rebooting the hard drive in a computer.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.040
Sometimes, the [drive] gets corrupted

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.900
and you don’t know exactly
where the problem is.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.540
But if you just turn
it off and reboot it,…

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.880
that corruption
[may get] cleared out.”

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.560
The evidence base started with
case reports, fasting followed by

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.520
a plant-based diet, remarkable reports
of years of pain and stiffness…

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.000
gone within a week, and,
more importantly,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.460
stayed gone on the healthier diet.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:03.060
One after another like that, but case
reports are just glorified anecdotes.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.880
There have been studies&nbsp;
going back decades suggesting

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.960
fasting may represent the most rapid,
available way to induce relief

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.980
of arthritic pain and swelling for
patients who have rheumatoid arthritis,

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.020
but the studies often failed to
have control for the placebo effect,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.740
which is especially important when
it comes to relying on self-reported

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.060
subjective symptoms such as
pain and general well-being.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.900
But there are objective measures,
lab tests of inflammation

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.180
that don’t appear to
be affected by placebos,

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.180
and that’s what you can
see in controlled trials,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.360
starting immediately and remaining
down for at least a year.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.560
Ten different measures of inflammation
significantly decreased

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.440
after the fasting and subsequent
meat- and egg-free diet,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.340
whereas none of the parameters
budged in those disease victims

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.980
that continued to eat their regular diets.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.300
And this squelching of inflammation
translated into a significant reduction

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.080
in pain, morning stiffness,
loss of grip strength,

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.140
and number of tender
and swollen joints.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.220
Even a year after the trial was over,
those who benefited from the diet

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.740
continued to benefit in
terms of pain, stiffness,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.180
and tender and swollen joints,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.000
presumably because they stuck with it.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.960
There is little doubt that while
fasting both inflammation and pain

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.160
are relieved, but if you go back to
the same diet you were on before,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.840
the inflammation returns—unless,&nbsp;
evidently, the fasting period

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.680
is followed by a vegetarian&nbsp;
diet. Why might that be?

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.460
It could be due to changes in the
microbiome,

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.300
the improvement in symptoms
coincided with a significant alteration

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.540
of the intestinal flora,
which may somehow be beneficial,

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:46.200
perhaps by strengthening the gut barrier.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.620
We know fasting can decrease
the leakiness of the gut

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.340
in rheumatoid arthritis patients,
but we don’t yet know what role,

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.560
if any, this plays in the disease process.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.420
It could be as simple as eicosanoids,
the mediators of inflammation

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.940
that are formed from
arachidonic acid.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.260
Arachidonic acid is a long-chain
inflammatory omega-6 fatty acid

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.940
found in animal fats.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.140
The biggest contributors
are chicken and eggs,

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:17.220
which together contribute
nearly half of American intake.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.840
That’s been suggested as an
explanation of why those eating

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.960
more plant-based appear to
have better mental health;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.260
they’re not suffering the
“cascade of neuro-inflammation”

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.200
caused by arachidonic acid;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.740
why removing eggs, chicken and other
meat was shown in a randomized

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.400
controlled trial to improve mood,
suggesting the arachidonic acid

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.300
might be negatively impacting mood
states and may help explain

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.780
the impact of more plant-based
diets on inflammatory diseases

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.700
like rheumatoid arthritis.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.820
So, that may help explain why
maintaining a plant-based diet

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:54.600
appears to be necessary “after
the fast to prevent the recurrence

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.700
of symptoms and
inflammatory activity,”

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.520
or as one popular
press article put it,

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.120
fasting may just be a tool to
get you to radically kickstart

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.340
a change in the way you eat.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.320
The strongest evidence of the benefits
of fasting surrounds the treatment

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.280
of an autoimmune joint disease
known as rheumatoid arthritis,

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.320
as I detailed in my last video.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:24.000
There was a German study suggesting
benefits for osteoarthritis as well,

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.520
with reported improvements
in pain and joint function,

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:30.840
but we'd really need randomized
controlled trials to know for sure.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.400
The researchers despair that
they only had 30 patients,

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.550
but that's 30 times more than
many reports on fasting

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:41.940
in the medical literature, which
may detail only single cases.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.760
For example, a woman with
a rare autoimmune disease

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.100
known as mixed
connective-tissue disease,

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:51.180
which can cause all sorts of painful
and distressing symptoms,

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.660
treated with steroids in an attempt
to suppress her immune system.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:59.400
But 21 days later, off her medications,
her symptoms improved with fasting,

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.740
and more importantly,
seemed to stay away.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:05.940
So, does fasting work for
mixed connective-tissue disease?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.980
Well, all we can say is, hey,
at least it worked at least once.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:14.940
A similar success story was reported
with fibromyalgia: a woman with

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.180
pain throughout her body, couldn't
sustain activity, on lots of drugs,

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.540
but ended up symptom
free 24 days later,

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.880
and remained that way
at least a month later.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:28.560
But when a modified fasting regimen
was tried on dozens of individuals,

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.600
the benefits seen at two weeks
largely disappeared by week 12.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.400
What about lupus?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.780
A 45-year-old woman remaining in pain
despite her immunosuppressive drugs,

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.580
but pain free by day four of fasting,
and remained symptom free

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:48.480
for a year, before wiping them
out again with a second fast.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.820
Now, note this wasn't just fasting,

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:55.140
but fasting followed by a plant-based
diet in an attempt to solidify the gains.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.560
And a strictly plant-based diet---
zero animal protein---alone

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.620
has been shown to control
symptoms in at least some cases.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:06.240
The same with sacroiliitis, a common
manifestation of ankylosing spondylitis,

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.420
an autoimmune arthritis that
primarily affects the spine,

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.240
causing back pain that
can last for years.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.780
They tried all sorts of conventional
therapies and drugs,

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.800
but the pain still didn't go away.
So, they tried recommending

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.660
the complete avoidance
of animal foods

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:26.760
and saw distinct persistent improvement
within days---until he ate meat again.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.680
But back on plant-based nutrition,

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:32.160
he was off most of his drugs, almost
completely free of symptoms.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.120
So at least in this case, inflammatory
pain refractory to other treatment

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:40.920
was abolished by eating healthier.
So, hey, at least it's worth a try.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:47.040
Autoimmune glomerulonephritis,
where your body attacks

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:50.340
your own kidneys, is a
common manifestation of lupus.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.700
In a case series of 29 patients
who were fasted for 60 hours

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.820
and then just put on fruits and
vegetables until they got better,

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:00.900
described such remarkable recoveries
that fasting, in their opinion,

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.300
should be an essential
part of treatment.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.380
What about multiple sclerosis,
an autoimmune nerve disease?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.800
Sufferers were randomized
to a fasting mimicking diet,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.760
meaning a modified fast that started
out with an 800-calorie-a-day diet

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:18.000
of fruit, rice, or potatoes, and
then they spent a week sipping

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.580
a few hundred calories of
flaxseed oil and vegetable broth

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.360
before transitioning to a
plant-based Mediterranean diet.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.040
And over the next three months,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.820
experienced a significant improvement
in overall quality of life.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:34.740
They also tried a ketogenic diet,
but that failed to offer clinically

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.720
or statistically significant
overall benefit.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:42.060
And finally, chronic urticaria,
hives, where you get a rash

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.940
of itchy weals and welts,
started to improve

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:48.540
on day three of the fast and
completely disappeared by day 11.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:52.740
This is consistent with studies out of
Germany and Japan that evidently showed

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:57.600
around a 75% effectiveness for
such patients with what looks like

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.360
some sort of tea with sugar diet.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.420
It's certainly worth giving
fasting therapy a try,

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:08.160
but of course fasting should only be
done under trained medical supervision.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.020
Otherwise you'd never know if you have
some hidden underlying kidney issue

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:16.800
that could land you in a coma
and then in the morgue.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.700
You have to have your kidney function
and electrolytes monitored

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.980
to make sure your body
is up for the challenge.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.140
Despite the potential benefits,

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.460
water-only fasting is not a cure or
treatment in the traditional sense.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:33.480
It's simply intended to promote the
body's self-healing mechanisms,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.840
since, by definition,
fasting is unsustainable.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:40.800
In order to maintain the results
obtained by water-only fasting,

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:44.700
it is necessary to adhere to a health-
promoting lifestyle that includes

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:49.362
a healthy diet of minimally processed
plant foods, sleep, and exercise.

